From: BaoFlash <dev@baoflash.local>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:51:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: ignore draggable regions in hidden WebContentsView

Port of upstream electron#51200 (c74de25) to the E39 tree: return HTNOWHERE
from NonClientHitTest() when the view is not visible, so a hidden
WebContentsView no longer contributes -webkit-app-region: drag areas to the
parent window's non-client hit test.

E39 adaptation: WebContentsView is itself a views::View here, so the guard is
GetVisible() instead of upstream's view()->GetVisible().

Verified on bao-v142-265-ppapi-sandbox+win-ppapi-process-sandbox with
WM_NCHITTEST over a hidden view that owns the only draggable region:
before HTCAPTION(2), after HTCLIENT(1); visible view still HTCAPTION(2).
---
 shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_contents_view.cc | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_contents_view.cc b/shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_contents_view.cc
index 64ae71a4de..e86940e858 100644
--- a/shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_contents_view.cc
+++ b/shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_contents_view.cc
@@ -82,6 +82,13 @@ void WebContentsView::ApplyBorderRadius() {
 }
 
 int WebContentsView::NonClientHitTest(const gfx::Point& point) {
+  // A hidden view must not contribute draggable regions to the parent window's
+  // non-client hit test, otherwise clicks over the area where a hidden view's
+  // `-webkit-app-region: drag` element would render still drag the window.
+  // Port of upstream electron#51200 (c74de25) adapted to the E39 class layout,
+  // where WebContentsView is itself the views::View (no view() accessor).
+  if (!GetVisible())
+    return HTNOWHERE;
   if (api_web_contents_) {
     auto* iwc = api_web_contents_->inspectable_web_contents();
     if (!iwc)
